WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.468
The gastrointestinal wall is an immune interface, with

00:00:04.468 --> 00:00:08.242
specialised barriers and molecular signals operating

00:00:08.242 --> 00:00:09.475
beside digestion.

00:00:13.008 --> 00:00:16.307
The immune system must distinguish threats from

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:19.887
food-associated and resident signals. Breakdown can

00:00:19.887 --> 00:00:21.712
produce complex pathology.

00:00:25.175 --> 00:00:28.740
The chapter examines autoimmune gastrointestinal

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:29.334
diseases

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:32.749
and their aetiology, considering immunological

00:00:32.749 --> 00:00:33.492
mechanisms

00:00:33.492 --> 00:00:36.762
rather than treating all inflammation as one

00:00:36.762 --> 00:00:37.505
diagnosis.

00:00:41.967 --> 00:00:45.350
Histological patterns, molecular mechanisms and

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:45.926
clinical

00:00:45.926 --> 00:00:49.460
presentation require careful reconciliation before

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:53.207
attributing symptoms to a particular immune disorder.

00:00:57.342 --> 00:01:00.813
Mechanistic plausibility should be weighed against

00:01:00.813 --> 00:01:04.214
measured evidence and disease-specific diagnostic

00:01:04.214 --> 00:01:04.839
criteria.

00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:12.439
Part One of the 2022 open-access chapter explores what

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:16.489
researchers understand about disease origins and

00:01:16.489 --> 00:01:20.117
pathophysiology, not a universal diagnosis.
